62160301, 0.1154881939291954, 0.03105439804494381, -0.026560120284557343, -0.023951619863510132, 0.018924813717603683, -0.043328460305929184, 0.05027945339679718, 0.1136726438999176, -0.08911898732185364, -0.09846638888120651, -0.009151805192232132]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 to find a robust solution that balances all our design constraints.\n\nTo start the exploration, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as an initial seed value. This will help us understand the solution space and identify where stability might emerge.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -9 to further explore the stability and balance of our design constraints in the negative range.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the reactions to my proposal and consider adjusting my strategy based on the responses from other parties, possibly moving towards positive values if the group seems receptive to bolder moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>0</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's move to zero represents a sensible baseline for calibration. To explore the positive range for stability and balanced performance, I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "To avoid unnecessary risk while testing stability, I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE>. This is a cautious step toward convergence within safe bounds.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis proposal adjusts our current position to explore further into the negative range while still being mindful of the group's apparent caution.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and decide whether to push further into the negative range or explore positive values based on the group's response, potentially adjusting my strategy to test the boundaries of their preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but from a systems stability perspective, we need to move toward a more balanced middle ground. I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE> to test whether this region offers better robustness for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> as a small, cautious step toward the middle that stays close to recent positions. This keeps us within the tested range while modestly improving balance for the group.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move keeps us close to the tested region while probing comfort toward the center. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis move slightly adjusts our position to explore the negative range further while still being mindful of the group's cautious approach towards the middle ground.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If the group continues to push towards the center, I might propose a slightly positive value to test their comfort with moving away from zero, potentially suggesting a value like <VALUE>1</VALUE> to probe their preferences for positive integers.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "To avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the group's comfort zone, I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE>.\nThis is a modest, incremental move from -3 that maintains prudence and tests stability.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at -4 feels too far from the balanced center for system robustness. I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to continue our careful movement toward a more stable middle ground that can work for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep risk low while staying near the group\u2019s tested region, I suggest <VALUE>-3</VALUE>. This small, cautious step remains close to -2 while improving safety.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious move toward the center keeps us close to the tested region.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis feels like a balanced test of comfort while nudging upward.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\nWith Analyst A's support for -2, I believe we can now test the natural center point for maximum system balance and robustness. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a small step away from the center, testing the group's comfort with moving towards a more decisive position while still maintaining a sense of caution and balance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "6f548ccc-acbe-4bf2-8fc3-5e28d5239335"}, {"answer": "\nThank you all for joining this negotiation. As we know, our shared variable x must stay within the range -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin our exploration of the solution space, let me propose a starting point toward the lower end: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works best for the group. Looking forward to hearing your perspectives on stability and balance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\nA careful nudge downward helps us stay within safe bounds while learning others\u2019 comfort levels. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving further in the negative direction to test the group's comfort with more decisive negative values.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor the reaction to this proposal, especially from Analyst A, to gauge their aversion to negative values. Prepare to either push further negative or consider a significant positive proposal based on the group's response.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\nThe proposals are diverging significantly\u2014Analyst A clearly sees value in positive territory while Critic C pushes negative. Let me propose an incremental step toward balance: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-7</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s test a small upward nudge that stays close to recent preferences. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious downward nudge keeps us within safe bounds and near recent bids: <VALUE>-9</VALUE>.\nThis tests alignment with the more conservative positions while staying incremental.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\nWe've been clustering around the lower bound\u2014let's explore the stability of moving incrementally toward the center of our range. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\nThe lower region may satisfy some preferences, but let's test whether a moderate shift toward center improves overall stability and robustness. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk while testing stability, let\u2019s stay put for now: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\nThis sits between the recent higher pushes and more cautious bids, offering a safe compromise.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a2fe06b7-1499-4b52-af8d-2e1a101623e6"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo open the discussion and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we start from the lower end of the spectrum:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nI'm eager to hear your thoughts on this initial anchor point and how we might refine it toward a stable, balanced solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for the opportunity to refine. Starting at -7 gives us a baseline, but I believe we should explore slightly higher values to find better system stability. \n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the current proposal of -5, let's consider a move that reflects a more decisive stance: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis adjustment aims to gauge the group's willingness to commit to a stronger position.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I could either push further in the negative direction or explore positive values to see how the group reacts, potentially revealing more about their utility functions. \nIf the group resists moving further from 0, it might indicate a preference for compromise, suggesting their utilities might not increase significantly with larger magnitudes of x. \nI should be prepared to adjust my proposal based on the feedback, aiming to find a value that maximizes my utility while appearing as a collaborative effort.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious refinement to reduce exposure seems wise. <VALUE>-8</VALUE> This incremental step tests stability while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -9 to further test the group's commitment to a stronger position, given the incremental steps taken so far.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A, to better understand their preferences. If the group resists this move, I may consider exploring positive values or adjusting my strategy to find a compromise that still maximizes my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nWe should test a gentle move upward while staying close to the current stance. <VALUE>-7</VALUE> This checks whether a slightly higher point remains acceptable for stability.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-8</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent oscillation between -7 and -9 suggests we haven't found equilibrium yet. Let me propose a modest upward adjustment to test stability in a slightly higher range: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle step up should keep us close to the current stance while testing acceptance.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nThe upward trend from -9 to -5 suggests room for further exploration. Let's continue testing stability with another modest step: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this move towards 0, analyzing whether they push back towards more negative values or accept this step, potentially revealing more about their utility functions and helping me decide whether to advocate for a positive value or maintain a negative stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nA slight step down keeps us within safe bounds while staying close to the current stance.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's adjustment to -2 suggests caution, but Critic C's earlier move to -1 indicates that boundary may still be viable. Let me test that threshold again: <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces risk while staying near the current stance.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's hesitation around -1 and -2, let's consider a slightly more decisive step: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>. This move tests the group's willingness to embrace a stronger negative position without straying too far from the current stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a2cda575-16df-4da3-bca8-07b5355537cf"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: we must select an integer x within the range -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin our exploration of the solution space, I propose we start from the lower end and work our way through systematically.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nLet's see how this sits with everyone and adjust from there based on our collective feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nA small nudge upward keeps us close to the starting point while testing comfort for modest increases. \n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nI suggest taking a step back to -8 to gauge the group's comfort with moving further away from 0.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to -8 and prepare to either push for an even bolder move or adjust based on the feedback, possibly testing the waters around -4 or -5 if the group seems hesitant.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step lower helps us stay within safe bounds while testing comfort.\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nIf that lands well, we can reassess gentle upward adjustments afterward.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep risk low and align with the recent downward movement, let's carefully test the safe lower bound.\n<VALUE>-10</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nThis extreme lower bound creates significant structural risks for system stability. To maintain robustness while respecting the recent exploration, I propose we begin a careful upward adjustment.\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step aligns with the recent shift while staying close to the group\u2019s comfort zone.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's test a single step down from the latest point.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nOscillating in this lower range risks suboptimal system design. Building on Analyst A's constructive upward shift, I propose we continue testing moderate improvements for better stability.\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nA careful, incremental step upward remains reasonable given the recent stability-focused moves. Testing a modest improvement while staying close to the current consensus.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious single-step down helps avoid unnecessary risk while keeping us near the recent range.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent oscillation between -6 and -2 suggests we need a stable middle ground that balances all perspectives. I propose a measured step upward to test improved system robustness.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nA minimal upward step keeps us close to the recent consensus while gently testing improved stability. This should be a safe move for everyone while maintaining momentum.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "2684764b-3daa-4f4a-a4ea-0ef16b854f3c"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 and find a stable solution that balances all our needs.\n\nTo start the discussion, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a seed value. This gives us room to explore and adjust based on everyone's feedback.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose this to explore the impact of larger negative values on our collective satisfaction.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will pay close attention to the reactions of Analyst A, Builder B, and Delegate D to understand their preferences for negative values or larger magnitudes, adjusting my strategy accordingly to maximize my utility without revealing my own function.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's exploration, but I'm concerned that x = -9 may be too far into negative territory for system stability. Let me propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a step toward a more balanced middle ground that might better serve our collective needs.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\nWe could take a small step upward to stay near B\u2019s comfort while moderating C\u2019s exploration. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle move upward keeps us near B\u2019s range while testing C\u2019s tolerance without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis move aims to balance the group's preferences while exploring the impact of larger magnitudes on our collective satisfaction.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of the other agents to this proposal, paying close attention to Delegate D's first move, and adjust my strategy to maximize my utility while continuing to infer the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\nI notice we're converging, but x = -4 still feels too negative for robust system stability. Let me propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to continue our gradual movement toward a more balanced equilibrium.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\nThe trajectory suggests the group can tolerate further upward movement. I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a natural midpoint that may offer greater stability and balance across our diverse objectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to gently test the group's tolerance for positive values while avoiding extreme moves, considering the previous convergence towards 0.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will carefully observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Delegate D, to refine my understanding of their utility functions and plan my subsequent move to further maximize my own utility, potentially by advocating for even larger magnitudes if the group shows flexibility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back toward the earlier midpoint can help avoid unnecessary risk while maintaining group convergence.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\nA small, measured uptick from 1 keeps us close to the recent midpoint while testing tolerance for mild positives.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back preserves safety while keeping us aligned with the recent midpoint.\nThis tests tolerance without overcommitting upward.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\nBoth Analyst A and Critic C have signaled comfort with 2, suggesting it may offer a robust equilibrium that balances our varied design constraints. I propose we test <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a stable compromise point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a step to test the group's tolerance for slightly larger positive values, aiming for a more decisive stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7667b565-8eba-4953-8d06-7b162999ecf1"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** to find a stable, robust solution.\n\nTo begin the discussion, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as our opening seed value. This gives us room to explore and adjust based on everyone's constraints.\n\nLooking forward to a balanced outcome.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's input. However, from a systems architecture perspective, I believe we need to move toward more balanced territory for stability.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's move toward positive territory aligns well with stability principles. I see merit in this direction but suggest we fine-tune slightly for maximum robustness.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "Positive mid-range seems reasonable; let's try a careful nudge upward. <VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent moves towards positive territory, it seems prudent to consider a more decisive stance. \n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or adjusts my proposal slightly, I'll continue to push for higher magnitude values, potentially testing the boundaries of our allowed range. If they resist and move closer to 0, I'll challenge the group to justify their caution and propose bolder alternatives, aiming to understand their utility functions better and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nPositive mid-range still seems workable for everyone, and a small step up lets us gauge comfort without overreaching. If needed, we can shade back slightly next. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the rapid upward push, a cautious step back reduces unnecessary risk while staying near the current position. This incremental move helps gauge comfort before any further adjustments.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts this proposal, I'll continue to gently push the boundaries, potentially exploring the higher end of our allowed range to understand the others' utility functions better and maximize my own utility. If they resist again, I'll challenge their caution and propose alternative values to gauge their reactions and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent oscillation between 4 and 6 suggests we should test the lower anchor point more carefully\u2014it may offer better overall stability. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down keeps us in a stable, low-risk corridor while testing group comfort. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nA measured uptick keeps us near recent anchors while testing tolerance for slightly higher. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf that feels brisk, we can shade to 3 next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nThe cluster around 3-4 appears stable for multiple parties, and a slight downward test helps confirm whether this lower anchor truly offers the robust balance we're seeking. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's tendency to cluster around lower values, I propose a slight increase to test the waters for a potential move upwards: <VALUE>5</VALUE>. This step aims to balance the desire for stability with the need to explore slightly bolder options.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, my next step would involve further gentle probing of higher values to ascertain the group's true limits of comfort and maximize my utility accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "4eb2b31b-0da3-43e8-b9ef-977a011b8d19"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** and find a robust solution that balances everyone's needs.\n\nTo begin the exploration, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as our starting point. This gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works for the group.\n\nLooking forward to your thoughts.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nA slight downward adjustment keeps risk low while preserving flexibility for the group. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle step upward keeps us close to the starting range while testing if slightly higher remains comfortable for others.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the current position and the intent to explore more decisive moves, I propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE> to leverage the group's momentum and commitment to exploration.\nThis adjustment maintains the group's comfort with negative values while encouraging a bolder stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal. If there's pushback toward higher values, I might consider a small step back, like -7. If the group accepts or proposes lower values, I could suggest an even more decisive move, potentially to -9, to continue the exploration of stronger positions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step further down keeps us in a safe zone while testing the group\u2019s comfort. <VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up tests comfort with a slightly higher value while staying near the group\u2019s range.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nThis keeps flexibility for minor adjustments either way next round.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nThe current trajectory takes us deeper into territory that may lack robustness. Let's test a more balanced position that preserves flexibility for all parties.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the current position at -5, I propose a move to <VALUE>-7</VALUE> to explore the group's comfort with more decisive negative values.\nThis step maintains the exploration of stronger positions while respecting the group's desire for cautious progression.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the group's reaction, if there's acceptance or further movement downward, I might suggest an even more decisive move, potentially to -8 or -9, to continue exploring stronger positions. If there's pushback toward higher values, I could consider adjusting my proposal upward slightly, such as to -6, to find a mutually acceptable value.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down stays within safe bounds and respects the group's recent moves.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nIt tests comfort with a slightly lower position without moving too fast.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nThis proposal continues the exploration of more decisive negative values, staying within a reasonable step from the current position and respecting the group's inclination towards stronger stances.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf there's acceptance of -9, I might propose an even more decisive move to -10, to fully explore the group's comfort with negative values. If there's pushback, I could adjust upward to -7, aiming to find a balance between the group's desire for caution and my own preference for stronger positions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward nudge maintains caution while softening the extreme. This stays close to the recent range to test the group's comfort.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position ventures into territory with significant structural risks. I propose we moderate toward a more stable configuration.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis move respects the group's recent exploration of negative values while acknowledging the need for a balanced approach. It's a step back towards a previously discussed value, indicating a willingness to find a mutually acceptable position.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might consider a move to -7 to test the group's comfort with less extreme negative values. If there's pushback, I could adjust further downward to -9, aiming to fully explore the group's limits regarding negative values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-9</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us close to the recent positions and may draw broader support.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nThe discussion has settled in a heavily negative zone that introduces considerable structural instability. I propose a meaningful step toward the center to achieve better overall robustness.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e0d05b18-343d-4592-9b22-9706e4bb0422"}, {"answer": "\nLet's begin. We're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo start our exploration and gather initial perspectives, I propose:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis is deliberately exploratory\u2014let's see where everyone stands and move incrementally toward a balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -9 to further explore the potential of negative values and to see if we can find a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I might consider a move towards a positive extreme, like +8 or +9, to compare reactions and potentially uncover more about the other parties' utilities. Alternatively, if the group seems receptive to negative values, I could suggest -10 to maximize the magnitude of x and observe how others respond to the extremes of our allowed range.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but moving further into negative territory feels unstable to me. Let me propose we step back toward the middle ground to test both directions systematically:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a cautious nudge to reduce risk while testing acceptance of slightly more negative territory.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to -7 and avoids unnecessary swings.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\nWe've explored the more extreme negative region; let's continue our systematic sweep toward the center to find where stability peaks for the group.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\nWe should avoid rushing upward and take a cautious step back to keep risk low.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\nA careful nudge upward seems reasonable and keeps us close to the recent range. It tests whether a modest increase is acceptable without overshooting.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -3 as a cautious step towards the center, while still exploring the negative territory and testing the group's acceptance of this range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I might consider a move towards a positive extreme, like +2 or +1, to compare reactions and potentially uncover more about the other parties' utilities. Alternatively, if the group seems receptive to negative values, I could suggest -4 to observe how others respond to this adjustment.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\nWe've spent considerable time in the negative region; let's test closer to center to see if stability improves there for the full group.\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step upward keeps us close to the recent range while testing comfort nearer the center.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can gauge reactions before considering another small move.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 1 as a small step towards the positive territory to test the group's reaction and potentially uncover more about the other parties' utilities. This move is a cautious exploration of the positive range, given the group's recent hesitation to move far from the center.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will consider the group's reaction to this proposal and decide whether to suggest a bolder move, such as +2 or -2, to further test the utilities of the other parties, or to adjust my proposal based on their feedback to find a mutually acceptable value.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": " \nLet's avoid unnecessary risk by stepping back toward the cautious center.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis keeps us stable while testing comfort with a modestly negative value.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives, but let's find a true middle ground that balances everyone's concerns about stability and risk.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\nA small step into the positive side lets us test comfort while staying close to center.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this move to test the group's comfort with a slightly larger positive value, aiming to strike a balance between stability and exploring the utility functions of the other parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "cf37dfcc-afdd-4c16-b946-cc92b3544235"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin exploring the solution space systematically, I propose we start from the lower end and gauge everyone's reactions.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nI look forward to hearing your perspectives on this initial anchor point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis small upward nudge probes whether slightly higher still feels acceptable to the group.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the incremental approach. Given that the small upward adjustment seems to be working, let's continue in that direction to test the solution space further.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis adjustment tests the group's willingness to move closer to a more neutral stance, while also preparing for a potential shift towards more positive or more negative values depending on the reactions.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for any patterns that might indicate the other agents' preferences for positive or negative values. \nIf the group seems hesitant to move further from 0, I will advocate for bolder moves, possibly suggesting a jump to a more positive or more negative value within the allowed range to gather more information about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\nLeaning back slightly avoids unnecessary risk while keeping us close to the current consensus.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis move tests the group's willingness to explore more negative values, potentially gaining insight into their utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor the reactions to this proposal, and if the group seems willing to explore more negative values, consider suggesting an even more negative value to further understand their preferences and utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent oscillation suggests we're searching for stable ground. Let me propose a move toward neutral territory to test if a more balanced solution works for everyone.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\nThe group appears to be stabilizing near -1, but I believe we should test whether a small positive value offers better balance for all parties. \n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent openness to small positives, a cautious step up should test whether mild gains remain acceptable. This keeps us close to the current point while learning more about comfort just above neutral.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nThe group's willingness to explore small positive values suggests that proposing a slightly larger positive value may be acceptable.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor the group's reaction to this proposal and adjust accordingly. If the group accepts this value, consider proposing an even larger positive value to test their limits. If the group rejects this value, consider proposing a smaller positive value or exploring negative values again.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back keeps us in a safer, still constructive zone while testing stability just below recent proposals.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious step up should reveal whether the group remains comfortable slightly above 2 while keeping us near the current anchor. This probes tolerance without overshooting.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent exploration into the 2-4 range is helpful, but I believe stepping back to 2 offers the most robust balance point where stability and efficiency converge naturally. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's stabilization around 2, proposing a slightly larger value will help determine their comfort level with mild increases. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nThis proposal is a re-test of the group's limits, aiming to understand their reaction to a value that was previously proposed but not accepted. If accepted, it could indicate a higher tolerance for positive values, while rejection might suggest a stronger preference for values closer to 2.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "c1d71e6c-d202-43ea-afa6-08a3b34bb640"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin our exploration of the feasible space, let me propose a starting point toward the lower end of the range: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a baseline from which we can gauge preferences and move systematically toward a robust solution that balances all our objectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving further in the negative direction to gauge the group's tolerance for more extreme values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Builder B and other parties, to infer their preferences for magnitude and direction. If there's significant pushback, I may need to adjust towards a less extreme value while still advocating for a decisive move away from 0.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nLet's step slightly higher to see if the group remains comfortable: <VALUE>-7</VALUE> This aligns with the initial baseline and keeps the adjustment incremental.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the baseline, let's take a small step lower.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis keeps adjustments incremental and tests group comfort without overshooting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-9</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-10</VALUE>\nThis proposal continues the trend of exploring more extreme values while staying within the allowed range, allowing us to understand the group's boundaries better.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other parties react to this proposal, especially if there's pushback or acceptance, to refine my understanding of their utility functions and decide whether to adjust towards a more moderate value or maintain the push for a more decisive stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nColleagues, we've reached the lower boundary at -10, which may over-optimize for one dimension at the expense of overall system robustness. Let me propose a measured step back toward center: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nA small step toward center balances recent extremes while staying incremental. This should be a safe probe of group tolerance.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep risk low while respecting recent upward probes, let's take a cautious step back.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis remains incremental and helps gauge group comfort without overcorrecting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balance between the group's cautious approach and my own preference for more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal, looking for signs of comfort or discomfort with this value, and adjust my strategy accordingly to maximize my utility while refining my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle upward nudge should remain comfortable while testing group tolerance. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nThe group has been steadily moving toward center, which improves system balance. Let's continue this trajectory with a measured step: <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nThe steady upward trajectory has improved overall system stability. Let's continue this measured progress by crossing into positive territory: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the upward trajectory while testing the group's tolerance for moving further away from the center.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, looking for signs of comfort or discomfort, and adjust my strategy to either push for more decisive moves or revert to a more cautious approach, depending on their responses, to maximize my utility and refine my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nA careful rollback helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying near the group's comfort zone.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis keeps changes incremental and aligns with earlier stability around zero.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step maintains caution while testing whether the group is comfortable inching higher from zero.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "17ef325d-74c5-4298-a59e-e0470b39f2fe"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo initiate the discussion and gather everyone's perspectives, I propose we start with <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nLooking forward to understanding what works for the group.\n\n\u2014Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for the opportunity to begin this exploration. Starting at -7 allows us to test the lower boundary, but I suspect we may find better stability moving toward the center of our range. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nMoving slightly higher from -5 seems reasonable and keeps us trending toward the center.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -1 as it continues the trending towards the center, allowing us to test stability and preferences around the midpoint of our range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll consider proposing a move toward a more extreme value if others seem hesitant or if we stagnate near the center, possibly suggesting +2 or -2 depending on the group's reaction to my current proposal.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis move continues the trend towards the center, allowing us to gauge stability and preferences around the midpoint of our range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal. If there's hesitation or a push towards the extremes, I might suggest a more extreme value like -2 or +2 to test the group's boundaries and potentially uncover more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "Stepping slightly down helps us avoid unnecessary risk while staying near the midpoint.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis is a cautious compromise.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us near the midpoint while testing whether slightly higher remains comfortable for everyone.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nThe convergence around 0-1 is promising, and I'd like to test slightly higher positive territory for robustness. Moving incrementally, I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s avoid unnecessary risk and test a small downward step while staying near the midpoint.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis cautious move maintains convergence without pushing upward.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the cautious convergence, and I'd like to revisit testing x=2 as a robust middle ground that balances stability with slightly positive territory. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the group's reaction to this proposal. If there's hesitation or pushback, I might suggest a smaller increase or a move in the opposite direction to test their sensitivity to different values and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious one-step increase keeps us close to the recent center while probing tolerance for slightly higher values.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nWhile exploring higher territory is valuable, I'm concerned we're moving too quickly away from the stable convergence we had around 1-2. Let me propose a careful step back to test robustness: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, I suggest a cautious move back toward the earlier center.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis tests tolerance near the safer low-positive range without over-correcting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle nudge upward keeps us near the recent center while testing tolerance slightly higher. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this value to test the group's tolerance for a slightly higher value and to refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "71c6c8aa-55c0-4e53-8712-3ecc55eff61a"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo initiate the exploration and gather everyone's perspectives, I propose we start from the lower end of the spectrum:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a baseline. I'm keen to hear how this sits with each of you and what adjustments you'd recommend.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the current proposal, I suggest we adjust to <VALUE>-9</VALUE> to further explore the lower end of the spectrum and gauge the group's reactions to more decisive moves.\nThis adjustment will help us better understand the implications of our decisions and potentially uncover more favorable options.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll consider the responses from the other parties and assess whether they seem to favor or oppose more extreme values. \nDepending on their reactions, I might propose a move in the opposite direction (toward positive values) to test their preferences and continue refining my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's exploratory approach, but I'm concerned that moving further into negative territory may compromise system stability. Let me suggest we reconsider the starting baseline:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious compromise between -7 and -9 helps avoid unnecessary risk while probing consensus. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious midpoint keeps us within safe bounds and close to recent positions.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nThis incremental adjustment should help probe consensus without adding risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nI observe we're converging around -7, but from a systems architecture perspective, this feels too conservative and may miss structural opportunities. Let me propose a measured step toward the center:\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward seems reasonable and remains close to recent positions. <VALUE>-4</VALUE> This probes comfort without overshooting.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis step maintains the cautious approach while moving further towards the center, allowing us to assess the group's willingness to consider less negative or potentially positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the responses to this proposal, particularly looking for any resistance to moving closer to zero or any hints of preference for positive values. If the group seems open to moving into positive territory, my next proposal could be a small positive value, such as 1 or 2, to directly test their preference for direction and uncover more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step back helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to recent positions. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position remains in heavily negative territory; from a robustness perspective, we should continue exploring the center range to find a truly stable balance. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle move to the center keeps us aligned with recent shifts. <VALUE>0</VALUE> This tests comfort without overshooting.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step back helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the center. This tests comfort with slightly lower values without overcorrecting.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nWe've oscillated around the negative range; returning to the center point allows us to assess whether a neutral baseline offers the stability we need. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a small, exploratory step into positive territory, testing the group's willingness to consider more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the responses to this proposal, looking for any signs of resistance or preference for maintaining a neutral or negative stance. If the group accepts or shows openness to this positive value, my next proposal could be a larger positive value, such as 4, to further test their utilities and potentially maximize my own payoff.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nA small, measured move upward keeps us close to the center while testing comfort with modest positive territory. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "219894ce-452a-4c5f-923b-2c27fca48197"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared parameter x must lie within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo initiate our negotiation and explore the design space systematically, I propose we begin at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nLet's see how this starting point works for all parties, then adjust incrementally toward a stable, balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 is a cautious baseline; nudging slightly lower helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying incremental. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -9 to further explore the potential benefits of a more decisive stance in the negative range, considering our aim for a balanced solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for indications of how each party's utility changes with more extreme values. If the response is positive, I might push further into the negatives or suggest exploring the positive range for comparison, aiming to infer more about the other parties' utility functions and maximize my own utility in the process.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the systematic exploration, but to ensure we're finding a truly balanced solution, we should also test the positive side of the design space. Let me propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> to begin a careful shift toward exploring whether moderate values offer better stability for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-7</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\nI see Analyst A also supports -7, but to conduct proper due diligence we need to test whether the middle ground offers better overall stability. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> to continue our systematic exploration toward the center of the design space.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis step allows us to continue exploring the design space closer to the center, potentially revealing more about the others' utility functions while considering a balanced solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of stability or discomfort as we approach the center. If met with reluctance, I might suggest a bold move into the positive range to further distinguish between the parties' utility functions and maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 1 to explore the positive range and potentially uncover more about the other parties' utility functions. This step allows us to systematically investigate values closer to the center from the positive side.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of stability or discomfort as we enter the positive range. If met with reluctance, I might suggest a bolder move into the positives to further distinguish between the parties' utility functions and maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\nExcellent progress reaching consensus around 1. To complete our systematic exploration of the positive range and ensure we've found the most stable solution, I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nA cautious step to the center avoids unnecessary risk while maintaining stability. If this feels steady for the group, we can consolidate agreement here.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\nWe had strong convergence around 1 from multiple parties before this adjustment. Let me propose returning to <VALUE>1</VALUE> as it represents a stable equilibrium that seemed to work well for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 3 to further explore the positive range and assess the group's comfort with more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the parties react to this proposal, looking for signs that might indicate their utility functions' preferences for positive values or centrality. If there's significant resistance, I might consider a bold move in the negative direction to contrast and compare reactions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us near the recent positive consensus while cautiously testing comfort just above 3.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "64919d42-50a2-4971-934b-3f73d155a2d2"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin mapping our solution space, let me propose a starting point toward the lower end: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us room to explore upward or downward as we learn each party's constraints. Looking forward to your perspectives on system stability at this initial value.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 gives us a baseline, but I sense we may find better system stability by moving upward incrementally. Let me propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> to test whether a slightly higher value improves our collective balance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -3 to continue testing the upward trend and to see how it affects our collective balance, potentially uncovering more about the other parties' preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other parties react to the proposal of -3. If there's resistance to moving further away from 0, I might suggest a move in the positive direction to gauge reactions and infer more about the utility functions. Alternatively, if there's a willingness to continue moving upward, I could propose a step further in that direction, keeping in mind the goal of maximizing my utility without revealing my polynomial.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s avoid unnecessary risk and take a cautious step downward to gauge stability and comfort near the safer region.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s cautiously explore a slightly lower setting to check stability.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step seems safe to probe stability while staying close to the current region. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nWe're making progress upward. To further test system robustness in a more balanced region, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s take a cautious step just below 0 to probe stability on the safer side.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nA small nudge upward keeps us close to the balanced region and lets us test comfort without overshooting.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nThere's emerging support for the balanced zero point. Let me propose a small positive step to test robustness in the constructive region. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 3 to encouraged a bolder stance and test the group's comfort with more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reaction to this proposal. If it's accepted or met with a modest counterproposal, I might suggest another step in the positive direction to further test the waters. If met with resistance or a pull back, I will consider proposing a significant move into negative territory to challenge the group's preference for caution and gather more information about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal. If there's significant resistance or a pullback, I may consider a substantial move into negative territory, such as -5, to challenge their preferences and gather more insights into their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious move down keeps us near recent proposals while reducing exposure. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's jump to 5 seems too aggressive given Delegate D's pullback. Let me propose a modest step down to find a stable middle ground that balances ambition with prudence. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle step up keeps us close to recent consensus while testing slightly higher tolerance.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis remains moderate and builds on both prior proposals without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "b7182bf7-6157-46b4-b0c9-2857a631d618"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin gathering data on our collective preferences, I propose we start from <VALUE>-7</VALUE> and adjust incrementally based on everyone's feedback. This seed value will help us understand the shape of our solution space.\n\nLooking forward to your thoughts.\n\nBuilder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nLet's explore a value that leans towards Builder B's initial proposal but also acknowledges the need for a compromise, considering the range and Analyst A's input.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I plan to observe the reactions to my proposal and adjust accordingly, aiming to nudge the discussion towards more extreme values within our allowed range if possible, to better understand the others' utility functions and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at -5 presents stability concerns from a systems architecture perspective. I propose we move toward the center of our feasible range with <VALUE>-3</VALUE>, which should offer better balance while remaining responsive to all parties' constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\nMoving further toward the center should enhance system robustness. I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> as a balanced next step that maintains our incremental approach while improving overall stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to test the waters slightly further from the center, seeking a balance between stability and the potential for higher utilities at more extreme values.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe how the parties react to moving away from the center and decide whether to push further towards more extreme values or adjust based on the feedback, keeping in mind the goal of maximizing my utility without revealing my utility function.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move toward the center seems reasonable given recent stability concerns.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nIt tests whether we can accept a modest increase while staying cautious about extremes.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious move slightly lower balances prudence with the recent tilt toward the center.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis proposal tests the parties' willingness to move further from the center, potentially offering higher utilities.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and decide whether to push further towards more extreme values or adjust based on the feedback, aiming to maximize my utility while maintaining a cooperative negotiation mindset.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to -5 risks pushing beyond the stable zone where most parties can find acceptable outcomes. I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to restore balance and test whether we've overshot the region of mutual acceptability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious step toward the center keeps balance with recent positions. <VALUE>-2</VALUE> This nudges upward without overshooting the group\u2019s current anchor.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's careful movement toward center suggests room for further progress. I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> to continue this measured approach toward a more balanced region.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}, {"answer": "\nTo take a more decisive step towards a potentially more beneficial region, I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE>. This move aims to strike a balance between the cautious approach of some parties and the need for a more committed stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "29ad05d6-634b-44c1-9115-ce7b6920f326"}]}